      "writtenOn": "2019-10-28T22:12:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you referring to the chip/npcx/espi.c guard clause?\n\nNote that, to date that guard clause has only included SLP_S3 and SLP_S4 virtual wires. Your patch would change that.\n\nNote also that the virtual wires other than SLP_S3 and SLP_S4 (and PLTRST, before this chain), are controlled by CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI.",
      "parentUuid": "5d322cc4_e8515f9b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2683,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2683,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "dadcadc7da9a270fa587af84415d8ef7e226a89e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e912cfc_2ebeb155",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2683,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-29T16:00:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "chip/npcx/espi.c only recently added the CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_SIGNALS guard around power_signal_interrupt().  My thinking was that the npcx eSPI driver needs to call power_signal_interrupt() anytime VW signals are enabled, so if additional virtual wires are added later, these guard clauses won\u0027t have to change.\n\nYou can skip creating CONFIG_HOST_ESPI_VW_ENABLED, but you should add a check that fails the build if CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S3 or CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S4 is defined and CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI is not defined.",
      "parentUuid": "72ac302e_c1e57c77",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2683,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2683,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "dadcadc7da9a270fa587af84415d8ef7e226a89e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94406bc7_d7f86edf",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2683,
