      "writtenOn": "2019-10-30T17:07:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I changed the name to reflect that the combined macro only reflects whether power signals are virtual wires. Per our OOB discussion yesterday, we don\u0027t want to call power_signal_interrupt for virtual wires we don\u0027t care about, which are enabled by CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI.\n\nDid you mean \"CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_ENABLED\" (as in, relating to the eSPI host command)? \"CONFIG_HOST_*\" is not much used. I guess this option also relates to the host per se, since that\u0027s where these power signals come from.",
      "parentUuid": "2e912cfc_2ebeb155",
